I keep seeing bad reviews for Attila. And, truthfully, I am not entirely sure as to why. The AI in both campaign and battles are very good, making it a struggle no matter who you play as. As for technical issues; I havent had any experience with bugs in Attila, but it certainly does not run well. I have a relatively medium end pc (I5 7400, 1060 6GB, 16 GB RAM), and can run at max graphics at 30fps. Generally, however, the graphics and animation quality make up for this. Somehow it looks prettier than Warhammer, despiter the latter coming out over a year later on a better engine.
Anyway, to sum up;
Very good Total War game, and definitely one of the best. Difficult for beginners, but very good for long-timers, and requires a NASA supercomputer to run. A solid 8.5/10

Honestly Hiveswap might not be the most amazing GAME. HOWEVER the story and work that has been put into making this thing is amazing and let me tell you, the story, the conversations, the small secrets hiding in plain sight. It just makes you want to click on everything and play it over and over again. <3
Thank you Hussie and everyone who helped make this, I'm looking forward to act 2!
