I'll start by saying that this is a good game, so yeah, I'd recommend it any day and I'd give it an 8.5/10. I really enjoyed playing this title by WB and Monolith, finishing it in about 29h with a 100% completion rate (struggled for a while to find a Ghûl Matron at 99%). What I have nice to say about it:
- The vibe is awesome, especially for a Tolkien's universe fan (LotR/Hobbit) ..also good for one if one has enjoyed AC and/or Prince of Persia, God of War series;
- Graphics are more than one could ask for;
- Fluid mechanics (for enhanced xp, use a controller);
- In terms of performance/engine the game doesn't have any optimization issues, barely encountered glithces of any type, so pretty good work on the quality assurance part as well;
- Rich in details, many interesting features and innovative elements;
- Immersive combat; fine weapons and skills, quite complex I'd say;
- Plenty of side quests;
Not a game you'd recommend to a beginner, not to say noob ^_^ (mind you, it can be challenging at times, and yes, you're going to die in this game, but that's not entirely bad now, is it?).
On the bad side, in order to progress, like one can see in many modern games, there is a clear sense of grinding going around, so the game itself can seem a bit repetitive at times, but one can live with it, no one asks you to go for gold digging (i.e. 100% completion); but you could as well adopt the road runner style and do the main story + some side quests in about 15-20h  and still have a lot of fun with the game.
- A thing that I'd call iritating it's the part where the 'AI' spawns like hell from nowhere and you are stuck in this never-ending battles because of the incoming hordes, especially frustrating when having to kill a boss.
- And one more thing regarding the 'AI' - they can be quite permisive when it comes to your stealth kills -> there are times when you are in a 20yd range but they can't see you after killing one of theirs as long as you keep sneaking...
Side mention: The DLCs are also fine.
And finally, I'd say that the price is more than excellent. So, Enjoy!
